From: g2code33 <269358183+g2code33@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 28 Sep 2026 16:24:34 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Add Force Move escape hatch for devices with persistently
 broken IndexedDB writes

completeSemester() can never succeed on a device where every IndexedDB
write fails (not just a cold-start hiccup) since its job is copying
bytes INTO IndexedDB. Add forceAdvanceSemester() which skips the
archive-copy step entirely and resets straight to a fresh workspace via
saveState() (localStorage-only, cannot fail the same way), then
best-effort releases the old semester's orphaned IndexedDB records.

Wire this into CompleteSemesterModal's error phase as a confirmation-
gated 'Force Move (Skip Archive)' panel that: exports a backup of the
current semester right from the dialog, requires the user to confirm
they've done so, then performs the move. The resulting success screen
points them at the pre-existing 'Import Semester Backup' feature on
the Academic Archive page to bring that exported file back in as a
normal browsable archive entry later.

Adds regression tests proving the move succeeds even when every
IndexedDB set/delete throws, that cleanup still runs opportunistically
when writes are healthy, and that it refuses to run without a student
profile.

Co-authored-by: arena-agent <297053741+arena-agent@users.noreply.github.com>
